                 rdfs:label "Maximum train current"@en ;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "stable" ;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> """For RINF XML data sets:
As long as the data provision through XML data sets is allowed, an XML attribute called â€œSetâ€ will be used to link the value of this parameter to the parameter 1.1.1.2.2.1.1 / ECS_SystemType"""@en .


###  http://data.europa.eu/949/maximumAltitude
:maximumAltitude rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                 rdfs:subPropertyOf :performanceDataParameter ;
                 rdf:type owl:FunctionalProperty ;
                 rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                               owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset
                                             :RunningTrack
                                           )
                             ] ;
                 rdfs:range xsd:double ;
                 :XMLName "IPP_MaxAltitude" ;
                 :applicable "Y/N" ;
                 :formatNote "[+/-][NNNN]" ;
                 :legalDeadline "In accordance with Implementing Decision 2014/880/EU and by 16 March 2019 at the latest"@en ;
                 :rinfIndex "1.1.1.1.2.7" ;
                 :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/MaximumAltitude> ;
                 :unitOfMeasure <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M> ;
                 <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2021-08-03"^^xsd:date ;
                 <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2022-10-20"^^xsd:date ,
                                                     "2024-09-19"^^xsd:date ;
                 rdfs:comment "Highest point of the section of line above sea level in reference to Normal Amsterdam's Peil (NAP)."@en ;
                 rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
                 rdfs:label "Maximum altitude"@en ;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "stable" ;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> """Normaal Amsterdams Peil (NAP), called also Amsterdam Ordnance Datum, it is a vertical datum commonly in use in Europe as reference level for the description of the height of objects in relation to the sea level.

The value of the parameter shall be given in metres, with tolerance of +/-100m."""@en .


